# Display-only identity mapping. Rewrites nothing in history — git applies this
# at read time (log, shortlog, blame), so old commits keep their original bytes.
#
# Four author identities accumulated over the life of this repo: an early short
# handle, a capitalised form of the same address, a school account, and the
# assistant identity that a handful of commits were made under. All of them are
# the same person, and `git shortlog -sne` split the contributor list four ways
# because of it.
#
# Bot identities (dependabot[bot], github-actions[bot], GitHub <noreply@github.com>
# on web-UI merges) are deliberately left alone: they are honest about who acted.

